    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "The validation of climate models predicting future Arctic sea-ice loss is challenged by an uncertain understanding of past sea-ice evolution during the analogous Pliocene warm period, a gap stemming from incomplete geological records from the region.",
    "method": "This paper reconstructs the emergence of modern Arctic sea ice cover by analyzing multiple geochemical proxies, including the IP25 biomarker and stable isotopes, from a Pliocene marine sediment core to determine the timing and extent of past sea ice conditions in the Atlantic-Arctic gateway.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct the long-term changes and emergence of modern sea ice cover in the Arctic Ocean during the Pliocene epoch using biomarker proxies (IP25 and GDGTs) from marine sediment cores.",
